# Source of truth

Read [MM-MCP-CF-Manager-Blueprint.md](MM-MCP-CF-Manager-Blueprint.md) before major features or when spec is unclear.

## Product constraints

- Electron desktop; TypeScript; React renderer; Tailwind 4; English UI only; MIT; no telemetry/analytics/ads.
- Cloudflare via official MCP `https://mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp` — **deterministic** service calls, not an LLM chat app.
- Do not replace MCP with direct REST without explicit blueprint change.
- No LLM runtime dependency for v1.
- Distribution: source folder + `run-app.bat` / desktop shortcut — **no** MSI/NSIS/electron-builder installer or portable EXE in v1.
- Node.js **24+** for dev/source-run; pin stable Electron (44.x baseline unless verified newer stable).

## Implementation order

Implement **Phases 1–7** (blueprint §24). Prove **one write path end-to-end** (`Purge Everything`) before expanding other writes (§29). Bulk must reuse the same services, not duplicated logic.

## Cursor must not

1. Store API token in plaintext on disk or SQLite.
2. Expose Node/MCP/DB to renderer.
3. Use unbounded bulk concurrency or `Promise.all()` for multi-zone mutations.
4. Enable write buttons before capability/permission is known.
5. Mark writes successful before Cloudflare confirms.
6. Log credentials or Authorization headers.
7. Invent Cloudflare/MCP behavior — verify official docs when implementing each service.

## Quality

Strict TypeScript; avoid `any` except isolated external boundaries. Small reusable components. Centralized English strings where practical. Tests **alongside** each service (§23.15–16).
